Your contribution to something big: 
 Explore how AI can transform software engineering and improve development workflows;
 Develop and experiment with autonomous AI coding agents and multi-agent architectures;
 Build AI-powered solutions for automated software testing and quality assurance;
 Explore how Large Language Models (LLMs) can understand and interact with complex software codebases;
 Develop intelligent engineering assistants using RAG, tool calling, and knowledge retrieval;
 Collaborate with experienced software engineers to develop prototypes and implement innovative AI solutions.
What distinguishes you: 
 Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, or a related field;
 Programming skills in Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, C++, or similar languages;
 Strong interest in AI, LLMs, and their practical applications in software engineering;
 Experience experimenting with AI coding tools, APIs, or AI-powered projects;
 Analytical thinking, problem-solving skills, and ability to work independently;
 Curiosity, creativity, and motivation to explore emerging technologies;
 Good communication skills in English, both written and spoken;
 Experience with AI coding agents, multi-agent systems, or personal AI projects is a plus.
Duration: 12 months
